      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nNow, let's simplify the terms inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the product of 14 and 456:\n\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to divide 6384 by 14:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\) is \\(\\boxed{456}\\).",
